  data: {
    LLM: "Keep your wild cards (7s and 2s) for when an opponent leads an Ace or Ten. Don't waste them on low-value tricks.\n\nIf you have multiples of a rank (e.g., three 8s), lead one. If someone tries to take it with a wild, you have two more 8s to win it back.\n\nTrack the wild cards. Knowing how many 2s and 7s are left determines how safe it is to lead a Ten to capture an opponent's Ace.",
